    "text": {
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:3/div:1/div:1/article:1/p:2": "Each site has its own gate. The Swimming Hole, David’s Dell and Twin Pines suit most vehicles; Silky Oak Flat and Pine Chapel are reached by a creek crossing and needs a 4WD.",
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:3/div:1/div:1/article:2/p:2": "Bring your own drinking and washing water, as well as a camp toilet.",
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:3/div:1/div:1/article:3/ul:1/li:2": "Portable toilet",
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:3/div:1/div:1/article:4/p:1": "Campfires are welcome in the provided fire pits. It can be arranged for firewood to be left waiting for your arrival during the booking process.",
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:3/div:1/div:1/article:4/p:2": "Never leave a fire unattended, drown it water before you sleep or leave, and check for total fire bans during the warmer months.",
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:3/div:1/div:1/article:8/div:1/div:1/span:2": "From 2:00 pm",
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:3/div:1/div:1/article:8/div:1/div:2/span:2": "By 10:00 am",
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:3/div:1/div:1/article:8/p:1": "Bryce lives on the property and is close at hand. Message him any time through Hipcamp if you have any questions or require anything during your stay.",
      "id:auto:guide.html:section:1/div:2/p:1": "Guest Guide & House Rules"
    },
